WEBVTT

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.550
We will now commence the operation

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.650
to cover the royal capital in a barrier!

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:11.210
Matthias, our best fighter, will be
too consumed with the barrier to engage!

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.480
The only ones who can protect the capital 
from attacking monsters and demons

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.620
are us, the wordless casters!

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.290
Give it your all, my students!

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:21.280
Yes, sir!

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.420
Report from communications team!

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.340
Magic detectors 25 and 26 
have picked up unusual activity!

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.170
It looks like a demon signature.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.060
Demon?

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.630
That's too soon to be a coincidence.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.050
Do you think someone 
leaked information about our plan?

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.400
If they had,

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.860
I don't think we'd be able 
to detect their casting so easily.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.730
We're probably picking up a demonic
transportation spell called Magiroad.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.730
I've got my hands full here.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.990
Can you two take care of it?

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:52.900
Eh?

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:29.000
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.000
<b>The Strongest Sage Leaves the School.</b>

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.560
It will just be the two of us, then?

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.150
Matty says we can do it, 
so we'll just have to trust him!

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.180
There it is!

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.230
Matty said that 
when the magic power starts swelling,

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.080
that's the sign the demons are coming!

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.380
So I guess we've got a little time?

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.270
We should take this time to get ready.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.440
<i>We've been running all this time...</i>

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.240
<i>How are they both fine?</i>

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:10.460
Use the special metal arrows you make 
for Alma against the demons.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.530
You can figure out what spells
to imbue them with yourself.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.960
Myself?!

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.610
In live combat, it's important 
to read the situation on the fly

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:21.090
and work out the ideal
casting circles for yourself.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.550
You'll be fine.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.180
I've taught you the techniques you need.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.230
I know you can do this, Lurie.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:30.580
I will!

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:37.840
It's finished!

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.150
Will these do?

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:43.540
They look good, as far as I can tell!

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.850
They seem pretty strong, too!

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.360
<i>She made her own casting circle?</i>

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.290
<i>And enchanted the arrows...</i>

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.020
<i>This is what Matthias's team is capable of?</i>

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.450
Alma!

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:56.240
Right!

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.670
Now!

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.630
I did it!

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.180
Alma, another's coming through!

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.540
Got it!

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.850
Guess I needed more than one...

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.240
Leave this to me!

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:21.080
Look! The Magiroad!

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:25.040
Guess there are no more
demons on the way!

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.370
And...

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.740
For the first time, just the two of us...

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.440
...pulled off a successful dispatch!

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.760
Did you feel that?

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.530
A big magic surge from the capital.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.210
We should get back!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.210
Yeah...

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.500
Let's hurry!

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.450
Great work on that dispatch, you guys.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.270
But the magic surge in the capital...

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.520
Don't worry.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.440
It's just what I expected.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.900
What does it mean, then?

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.240
It's a more advanced version of Magiroad,

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.260
that sacrifices a demon 
to achieve long-range travel.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.860
But demons have no spirit
 of self-sacrifice,

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:10.530
so they probably sacrificed the weakest 
of their group to feed the spell.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.220
What should we do?

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:18.000
The demons will likely appear 
above Second Academy.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.520
The barrier will take a little more time 
to get ready,

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.630
so I'll need you 
to buy time until then.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.920
We will! We'll do our best!

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.400
Let's go, Lurie!

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.260
Yes!

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:32.100
<i>Maybe it's because they've
gained confidence in battle...</i>

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.010
<i>There's no more hesitance in their tone.</i>

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.250
Forty boxes of mithril!

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.650
That should do it!

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.860
Well done, Iris.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.820
Mr. Headmaster!

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.370
Excellent timing.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.470
Matthias left these for you.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.700
Magistones for casting circles?

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:57.470
Matty got me this much 
so that I won't have to worry if I mess up...

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:00.080
I'll make sure it works!

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:03.820
Massive magic readings detected 
above the academy!

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.430
Into formation, all of you!

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.480
That seems to have gone well.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:21.310
The demon's... here?

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:25.390
Oh? You intend to fight me, do you?

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:27.630
What a foolish bunch of humans...

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.950
Force of numbers won't change your fate.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:33.990
I'll send you all 
to the grave together!

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.680
How easy.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.910
I thought I was a goner!

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.420
It really blocked it!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.280
Matthias's defense spells are the best!

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:55.180
Those wretched humans blocked my spell?!

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.620
Now! Crest of Standard! 
Crest of Lesser!

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:58.640
Sir!

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.740
It's no use! We can't reach him!

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.030
In that case...

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.690
You don't have much 
in the way of attacks.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:11.950
He's way tougher 
than those earlier demons.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.250
Lurie! How's that enchantment coming?

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:18.020
You okay?

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:20.610
This casting circle is quite complex.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.850
Could you buy me a little more time?

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:24.140
Sure thing!

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:28.050
How long can you hold out against this?!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.100
We'll endure whatever you throw at us,

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.130
until Lurie's enchantment is done!

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.920
You may have learned wordless casting,

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.100
but you can't surmount
the difference in our power!

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.050
That's more powerful than the last one!

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:43.690
But we'll hold it back!

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.010
Another failure...

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:49.030
Where's the next...

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:54.860
<i>This is... the last piece...</i>

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.620
What happened 
to all that confidence of yours?

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:00.900
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:03.460
<i>If this keeps up, 
he'll break through our spell!</i>

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.030
<i>What will I do?</i>

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.050
<i>If this fails, they'll all...</i>

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:15.500
<i>I was able to succeed in the past 
due to Matty's support.</i>

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:18.970
<i>But all on my own, I...</i>

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.160
We will hold him back!

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:23.060
Until Lurie's enchantment is complete!

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:29.070
<i>But they're all... 
Matty is... counting on me!</i>

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.440
Keep going, Lurie!

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.030
I will! 
I will make it work!

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.120
I did it! Alma!

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:48.750
Thanks a bunch, Lurie!

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.880
Leave the rest to me!

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:55.790
It works only if it hits!

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:57.970
I won't let Lurie's hard work 
go to waste!

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.190
Now!

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:04.200
Yes, sir!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:12.880
We did it!

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.480
We really did it!

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:15.900
We defeated a demon!

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:18.060
We can do it, too!

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:23.870
Oh? You took out Belias...

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:25.450
There's another demon?!

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:27.830
But it's only one! We can still—

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:33.210
Its attacks are more powerful 
than the last one's!

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:44.710
I told him to wait 
until we were all ready.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:47.480
There's plenty of slaughter
to go around, after all.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.310
Right, everyone?

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:52.000
It can't be true...

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.900
There are so many...

00:09:58.380 --> 00:09:59.910
You can't do it, Alma!

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:03.130
It took everything we had 
just to beat one!

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:06.780
But we have to buy time 
until Matty arrives!

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:16.670
We don't want Matty 
to be disappointed in us.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.040
Lurie...

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.250
Look at all those happy faces.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:28.520
I know. Let's compete 
to see who can kill the most!

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:31.980
The slaughter begins.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.980
The <i>what</i> begins?

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:40.110
Sorry, but you're the ones 
facing a slaughter.

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:44.080
That's a bigger turnout than expected.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.790
Impossible. His aura is inhuman.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:50.290
Are you the one who killed Alias?

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.820
Matty!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:57.800
Now, choose!

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:01.220
Will you die begging pathetically 
for your lives?

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.160
Or will you fight 
and die in humiliation?

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:13.380
So you know, 
both choices mean you die.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.980
Don't underestimate us! 
You're still just a human!

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:20.200
You can't beat a demon 
at its full power!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.530
Such determination.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:25.710
I'll grant you an exit 
suited for a villain's role.

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:39.210
Dispatch successful.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:40.800
Matty!

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:45.350
This body's reached a level 
where it can fight decently, I suppose.

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:54.250
Matthias! You did very well.

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.340
I'm just glad you're all safe.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:57.900
That was amazing, Matty!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:00.590
You beat them all in a flash!

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:03.780
Yes, thanks to the sword Lurie made.

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:05.410
Thank you.

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:07.990
It's nothing...

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.200
You too, Alma.

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:11.790
Thanks for buying time.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:13.640
That's right!

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:15.360
Did you finish the barrier?

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.300
Yes, I finished digging the hole 
for the barrier.

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:21.010
Iris and the others are handling the rest.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.890
You've all done very well.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.970
Now we add in the magistone, 
and it's done.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.310
I'm hungry!

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.460
What is that?

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:47.160
Papa! The sky is so pretty!

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.330
We did it!

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:58.850
It went perfectly!

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:01.550
We aren't finished yet.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.870
The fun's just getting started, in fact.

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:07.590
But we activated the barrier, didn't we?

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:10.620
And I feel a lot 
of magic power from it...

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:13.920
This magic power isn't from the barrier. 
It's from monsters.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:15.810
A ton of them.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:17.010
Monsters?

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:22.690
Do you mean the spell that the demons 
set up before to summon monsters?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:23.800
That's right.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:27.170
That magic power and the power 
from the demons we defeated

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:31.520
traveled along the school's Dragon Vein 
and had a good influence on it.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:33.000
"A good influence"?

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.040
Don't tell me...

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.000
It's going to be a bigger horde 
than we expected.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:38.580
Students!

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:42.020
The barrier will keep the capital safe,

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:44.130
but not the surrounding towns!

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:47.220
We have to stop all the monsters here.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.450
My students, fight your hearts out!

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:51.560
Yes, sir!

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:02.940
What the...

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:05.630
It's the trap Matthias mentioned!

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:09.010
Wow. We're really tearing 
through those monsters!

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:11.530
It seems that the traps 
and magic items we set up

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.990
are sparing them a lot of fighting.

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:19.580
And the students of Second Academy 
have improved vastly in these last few months.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.040
They won't lose to monsters 
of such a low level.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:28.460
Hey, there's a bigger one on the way.

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:31.140
Yes, with a Dragon Vein like that,

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:33.840
there's a second wave for sure.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.860
All forces, retreat! Hurry!

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:39.940
We'll take over here.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.590
Thank you!

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:43.370
Are you three ready?

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:44.020
Yes!

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:45.740
Iris, take the front line.

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:47.200
Yes, I shall!

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:47.990
Hold it.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.180
This way's faster!

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:58.710
That wasn't nice, Matthias!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.740
I did it!

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:03.880
Great work, Alma!

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.680
I'll get in there, too!

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:10.010
<i>Having a proper team 
makes combat so efficient.</i>

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:13.910
<i>Now I can focus 
on the more powerful enemies.</i>

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:16.930
That monster...

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.710
Matty! I'm picking up 
the strangest magic readings...

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:20.890
Hey, what's that?!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:26.760
A monster known as a Void Eater, 
which devours monsters around it to grow.

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:28.620
It's my first time ever seeing one.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:30.900
Shouldn't we defeat it 
while it's still small?

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:34.450
Actually, let's let it absorb 
all the monsters in the area.

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:36.200
It'll save time in the long run.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:41.360
I think it's trying to absorb me, too.

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:44.630
It shouldn't be powerful enough 
to absorb you.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:49.010
It's just about finished, so let's give it
a hand with the finishing touches.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:54.140
Lurie. Carve this pattern into a magistone 
and throw it at the Void Eater.

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:55.440
I will.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:58.860
Absorption-type monsters evolve 
in a distorted way,

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:00.810
so they don't provide good materials.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.920
So we'll use a casting circle 
to drive its evolution in a particular direction

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:06.150
and acquire worthwhile materials from it.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:08.290
You're really assuming we win this, huh?

00:16:08.290 --> 00:16:09.970
The inscription is done!

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.060
I'm throwing it in!

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.740
And here go a few more!

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:18.590
Eat up! Grow big and strong!

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.380
M-Matty...

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:42.560
Are you totally sure about this?

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.280
It's looking good.

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:48.820
Its overall magic power is stable, 
and we'll get lots of experience from it.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.090
Experience?

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.740
You're <i>really</i> assuming we win this, then...

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.700
I-It's coming closer!

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:59.090
Okay, let's beat it!

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:01.890
As usual, 
Alma and Lurie will attack with arrows.

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:04.360
Iris, aim for its feet.

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:05.860
Sure thing!

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:10.570
But Matty, you can't have 
much magic power left!

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:11.630
That's all right!

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:15.970
<i>I've just about got the muscle memory 
for how a Crest of Failure fights!</i>

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:27.010
<i>The best way to deal quick damage 
to a large creature like this</i>

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:29.400
<i>is to tick it off!</i>

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:40.050
Special Magic Enchant!

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:44.000
It's working!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:45.580
No...

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:48.870
Its legs are regenerating!

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:53.260
If that won't work, I'll give it 
all the enhancement spells I can!

00:17:58.050 --> 00:17:59.190
And...

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:02.950
A Special Magic Enchant, times two!

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:05.900
It regenerated again!

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.020
I'm not done yet.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:15.440
<i>This kind of thing is 
where the Crest of Failure really shines.</i>

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:20.720
<i>This spell will last until either I run out 
of magic, or the enemy dies.</i>

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:25.580
And now... the finish!

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.340
Dispatch successful!

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:37.800
You beat it?

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:40.890
Yeah, I don't think it'll regenerate again!

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:43.110
It's okay to come closer.

00:18:43.110 --> 00:18:44.600
Well done, all of you.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:48.140
Well done, Matty!

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:51.890
Building up a barrier, 
then dispatching monsters and demons...

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:54.000
Even I'm a little tired after all that!

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.640
Just "a little"?

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:00.430
And I'm just hungry!

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.310
Matty?

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:27.580
Is something the matter?

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:32.320
Well... this creature's appearance 
suggests a truly intere—

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:35.820
er, a potentially dangerous Dragon Vein.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:39.940
I think I'll have to look 
at some dungeons outside the capital.

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:41.910
<i>So he really is...</i>

00:19:49.650 --> 00:19:51.410
So you're leaving the academy, eh?

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:54.380
Yes. I'd like to do a survey 
of Dragon Veins.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:57.430
I thought you'd say that someday.

00:19:57.430 --> 00:20:02.270
I hate to say it, but there's nothing left 
for you to learn here.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.770
But I don't intend to expel you.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:11.280
I'd like to keep you on our rolls 
with a special scholarship.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:16.440
The school will have greater freedom 
for more effective growth

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.940
with your achievements under its belt.

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:22.690
And if you find yourself in trouble, 
it'll be easier

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:26.330
for me and the nation to intervene 
on your behalf if you're a student.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.660
I think it's a good deal for both of us.

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:32.970
Indeed. It's not a bad offer.

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:35.040
I think I'll take it.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:37.450
I'll prepare the documentation, then.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:42.090
Matty... 
You're really leaving the school?

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.190
Lurie...

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:47.210
If you'd like to go off with Matthias,

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:51.270
I can give the rest of you 
a scholarship as well.

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:53.130
Us, too?

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:58.060
Well... Only if they want to...

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:00.720
I'll take a scholarship!

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:04.580
Matty has so much more to teach me 
about enchantment spells!

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:09.120
Me, too! I want to go on a journey 
and become an even better archer!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:11.660
If you're all going, I'm in!

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.310
Seems that it's all decided, then.

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:25.550
Thank you for everything, Headmaster.

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:27.430
Likewise!

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.600
Drop by any time you wish.

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:33.060
Second Academy will be here 
for you any time.

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:34.460
Right!

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:36.280
All right, let's go.

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:38.110
See you guys again someday!

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:39.560
We're off!

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:41.520
Bye-bye!

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:46.240
It's so exciting! 
Like starting a new adventure!

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.160
Indeed!

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.880
Wonder if we'll find some tasty food!

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:50.640
I'm hungry!

00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:28.090
Iris, are you all packed for the trip?

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:31.250
Yes! My possessions include 
these big iron dumbbells...

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:33.050
One cow for eating...

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:35.430
And this body pillow I made 
out of a monster corpse!

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.580
You won't need that on a journey! 
Throw it away!

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Episode 7
The Strongest Sage Goes on a Journey.</b>

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:39.930
But why?!
